     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Reflexion lessons — CRUD + relevance ranking.
     3	
     4	Sprint 3 Item A. Implements Shinn et al. 2023 "Reflexion" pattern for
     5	the ceo-orchestration framework. When a benchmark scenario fails, the
     6	runner writes a lesson file. When an agent is spawned, the top-3 most
     7	relevant lessons are injected into the prompt.
     8	
     9	## Lesson storage
    10	
    11	Each lesson is a JSON file under:
    12	
    13	    $HOME/.claude/projects/<slug>/lessons/<lesson_id>.json
    14	
    15	Lesson IDs are SHA-256 hashes of (scenario_id + created_at). Files are
    16	human-readable JSON, one per lesson.
    17	
    18	## Relevance ranking
    19	
    20	    score = archetype_match × scope_overlap × recency_decay
    21	
    22	- archetype_match: 1.0 if exact match, 0.3 if related, 0.0 otherwise
    23	- scope_overlap: Jaccard similarity of lesson scope_tags vs task keywords
    24	- recency_decay: exp(-days_since_lesson / 90) — 90-day e-folding time
    25	  (half-life ≈ 62.4 days; PLAN-154 A14 docstring fix — the old
    26	  "90-day half-life" wording overstated retention)
    27	
    28	Top 3 by score, capped at 2K total tokens of injected content.
    29	
    30	## PLAN-154 — gated learning loop (candidate lifecycle)
    31	
    32	Distiller-proposed lesson CANDIDATES live in a separate namespace,
    33	``<lessons_dir>/candidates/<lesson_id>.json``, so no legacy reader
    34	(``list_lessons`` / ``get_top_k`` / ``build_index`` / prune / ranker)
    35	can ever surface a non-approved candidate into a spawn prompt.
    36	
    37	State machine (zero self-activation — constraint 5):
    38	
    39	    add_candidate() ──> PENDING ──/lesson-review approve──> APPROVED
    40	                          │  │
    41	                          │  └──(TTL 30d)──> EXPIRED      (terminal)
    42	                          └──(scan hit / scanner down /
    43	                              tamper at approve)──> QUARANTINED (terminal)
    44	
    45	- The promotion boundary is fail-CLOSED (A4): injection-scanner
    46	  unavailable OR scan hit at ``add_candidate`` → QUARANTINED.
    47	- Approval events in the HMAC chain carry
    48	  ``sha256(trigger + "\\n" + advisory_text)`` (A6). Renderers verify
    49	  the recomputed hash against the chain BEFORE rendering; the chain —
    50	  not this mutable ``$HOME`` store — is the integrity anchor.
    51	- Every time function takes an injectable ``now_fn`` (A9); the wall
    52	  clock is only the default.
    53	- Candidate vocabulary is bounded (A5): advisory_text ≤ 200 chars, no
    54	  backticks, no newlines, no control chars; trigger/scope_tags are
    55	  closed-character-class tokens.
    56	
    57	## CLI
    58	
    59	    python3 lessons.py write --scenario-id X --archetype Y --remember "..." --scope "tag1,tag2" --agent-response "..." --expected "..."
    60	    python3 lessons.py top3 --archetype Y --keywords "tag1,tag2"
    61	    python3 lessons.py list
    62	    python3 lessons.py prune --older-than-days 180
    63	    # PLAN-154 candidate lifecycle:
    64	    python3 lessons.py add-candidate --trigger t --text "..." --scope "a,b"
    65	    python3 lessons.py candidates [--status PENDING] [--json]
    66	    python3 lessons.py approve <lesson_id>
    67	    python3 lessons.py expire-sweep
    68	
    69	## Constraints
    70	
    71	- stdlib-only, Python >= 3.9
    72	- Directory scan capped at 1000 files (debate consensus R-DEV3)
    73	- All agent_response content passes through _lib.redact before storage
    74	"""
    75	
    76	from __future__ import annotations
    77	
